@startuml
title Kids Flashcards - PostgreSQL ERD
hide circle
skinparam linetype ortho

entity "flashcard_sets" as Sets {
  * id : UUID <<PK>>
  --
  * name : varchar(120)
  * description : varchar(2000) = ''
  * created_at : timestamptz
  * is_public : boolean = false
  owner_subject : varchar(200)
  owner_account_id : varchar(200)
}

entity "picture_uploads" as Uploads {
  * filename : varchar(100) <<PK>>
  --
  * owner_subject : varchar(200)
  * owner_account_id : varchar(200)
  * created_at : timestamptz
}

entity "flashcards" as Cards {
  * id : UUID <<PK>>
  --
  * set_id : UUID <<FK>>
  * position : integer
  * front_type : varchar(5)
  * front_content : varchar(10000)
  * front_instruction : varchar(2000) = ''
  * back_type : varchar(5)
  * back_content : varchar(10000)
  * back_explanation : varchar(2000) = ''
}

Sets ||--o{ Cards : contains / ON DELETE CASCADE
Cards ..> Uploads : image content URL (logical reference)

note left of Sets
  Ownership uses Life2 subject AND accountId.
  Identifiers are assigned from verified JWT claims.
  No local user/password table or Life2 database FK.
  New series are private by default.
  Public series: readable by anyone, owner-only edits.
  Private series: owner-only reads and edits.
  can_edit is computed per caller, not persisted.
  Nullable owners preserve legacy data during migration;
  private unowned rows are inaccessible until assigned.
end note

note right of Uploads
  New uploads record their authenticated owner.
  Files reside on disk, outside PostgreSQL.
  GET permits a visible series reference or upload owner.
  Legacy images remain protected by series visibility.
  Image URLs are logical references, not foreign keys.
  Set/card deletion does not delete files or metadata.
end note

note right of Cards
  UNIQUE(set_id, position), deferrable.
  position is zero-based within a set.
  Face types are constrained to text or image.
  Optional captions are stored as empty strings.
  Reordering submits every card ID exactly once.
  Image content references an uploaded picture URL.
  Pictures reside on disk, outside PostgreSQL.
  Flip state and animation are transient browser state.
  Interface language is a browser localStorage preference only.
  Set/card content and captions are never translated.
  Set ID and mode appear in browser paths; mode is not persisted here.
  Opening from the library defaults to Practice.
end note
@enduml
